    (60,'A VAE learns a shared latent space between pre-trained generative models, enabling unsupervised cross-modal transfer such as image to audio and bridging VAE/GAN models. A linear classifier imposes semantic alignment while preserving locality. The hierarchy separates base-model training from personalized alignment retraining.',[r'(VAE|variational)',r'latent',r'(modal|audio)',r'(classifier|semantic)',r'(locality|local)',r'(retrain|hierarch|personal)'],'How is semantic alignment imposed across the shared latent space?',[r'linear',r'classifier']),
    (61,'AITL combines adversarial domain adaptation and multi-task learning to address both genomic-input and drug-response-output discrepancies between preclinical cell-line and clinical patient data. With limited clinical outcomes, it outperforms tested pharmacogenomics and transfer-learning baselines; the possible oncology benefit is not a clinical deployment result.',[r'AITL',r'adversarial',r'multi.task',r'input',r'output',r'(limited|clinical)',r'baseline'],'Does AITL address only the input-space discrepancy?',[r'(both|input.*output)',r'output']),
    (62,'An end-to-end joint entity/relation extractor integrates a large pre-trained language model and self-attention without external NLP tools. Pre-training and avoiding recurrence make it fast to train. Across five datasets and three domains it matches or exceeds state-of-the-art results.',[r'(entity|entities)',r'relation',r'pre.trained',r'(without.*external|no.*external)',r'(five|5)',r'(three|3)'],'Does the proposed joint extractor require an external dependency parser?',[r'(without.*external|no.*external|does not.*external)']),
    (63,'A variational Bayes RNN scheme adapts truncated backpropagation through time for uncertainty estimates and regularization at small extra training cost, reducing parameters by 80 percent. Local-gradient posterior sharpening improves Bayesian networks more broadly. Bayesian RNNs outperform traditional RNNs on language modeling and image captioning, and an uncertainty benchmark is introduced.',[r'(Bayes|Bayesian)',r'(truncated|backpropagation)',r'80',r'(gradient|sharpen)',r'caption',r'(language|benchmark)'],'What information is used to sharpen the posterior approximation?',[r'local',r'gradient']),
    (64,'An autonomous-drone case study compares TrailNet, InceptionResnet and MobileNet on accuracy, robustness, power and inference time, describing software/hardware and implementation details. MobileNet performs better with less computation and power in the study; further safety and performance improvements remain future work.',[r'MobileNet',r'TrailNet',r'Inception',r'power',r'(inference|time)',r'(study|future|safety)'],'Which model had lower computation and power requirements in this case study?',[r'MobileNet',r'(power|comput)']),
    (65,'A modified relative-attention Transformer reduces intermediate memory from quadratic to linear in sequence length. It generates minute-long music, motif continuations and melody-conditioned accompaniments. Evaluation uses JSB Chorales and Piano-e-competition, with state-of-the-art performance on the latter.',[r'Transformer',r'relative',r'quadratic',r'linear',r'(minute|motif|accompaniment)',r'Piano'],'What memory-complexity change enables longer compositions?',[r'quadratic',r'linear']),
    (66,'Width-based lookaheads are extended to Stochastic Shortest Path problems under restricted compute budgets by estimating costs-to-go. The work formalizes them as rollout algorithms, defines SSP width and sample complexity, and outperforms UCT and RTDP in the tested SSP benchmarks.',[r'width',r'(Stochastic Shortest|SSP)',r'costs?.to.go',r'(budget|restrict)',r'UCT',r'RTDP'],'Which quantity is estimated to overcome poor performance on SSP problems?',[r'costs?.to.go']),
