    (68,'Generative DPP uses a determinantal-point-process kernel to measure real and generated diversity, then penalizes diversity mismatch to resist mode collapse without changing the original training scheme. Embedded in GAN and VAE training, it improves tested data efficiency, convergence and quality on synthetic and natural-image datasets.',[r'(DPP|determinantal)',r'diversity',r'(mode.collapse|collapse)',r'(without.*chang|unchanged)',r'(GAN|adversarial)',r'(VAE|variational)'],'Does the diversity penalty require changing the original training scheme?',[r'(without.*chang|unchanged|does not.*chang)']),
    (69,'A unit-wise-capacity complexity measure gives a tighter generalization bound for two-layer ReLU networks and a matching Rademacher-complexity lower bound. Correlation with test error as network size increases, within the reported experimental range, could partly explain improved generalization with overparameterization.',[r'unit.wise',r'(two|2).layer',r'ReLU',r'Rademacher',r'(range|experiment)',r'(partly|partial|could|may|suggest)'],'Does the result establish an unrestricted guarantee for arbitrarily deep networks?',[r'(two|2).layer',r'(range|experiment|partly|could)']),
